    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.77,
      "end_seconds": 149.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.99,
      "end_seconds": 155.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "alright, have you noticed milky nipple discharge, palpitations or headaches?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.13,
      "end_seconds": 160.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "No, um, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.31,
      "end_seconds": 166.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.4,
      "end_seconds": 173.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.32,
      "end_seconds": 192.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Okay, I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.65,
      "end_seconds": 201.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.58,
      "end_seconds": 234.56,
      "duration_seconds": 11.98,
      "text": "Okay: BMI works out to 18.3, height 178 centimetres. And weight 58 kilos, temperature 36.8, heart rate 68, BP is 119 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.08,
      "end_seconds": 236.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.94,
      "end_seconds": 240.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "We'll look at it together shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.74,
      "end_seconds": 245.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.3,
      "end_seconds": 250.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.95,
      "end_seconds": 269.65,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Your weight is up a little, and there is acne on the jaw and some coarse hairs on the chin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.84,
      "end_seconds": 283.25,
      "duration_seconds": 8.41,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So where does that leave us? I'd lean towards polycystic ovary syndrome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.66,
      "end_seconds": 290.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.57,
      "end_seconds": 319.69,
      "duration_seconds": 28.12,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with polycystic ovary syndrome do well once it's treated properly. A thyroid test is what I'd like next, for irregular periods. Let's use metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, long term. It's for polycystic ovaries. Regular exercise and a lower-sugar diet help the periods settle. Come back after the results."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.28,
      "end_seconds": 323.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Yes, that's manageable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.64,
      "end_seconds": 329.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.1,
      "end_seconds": 338.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Okay, so good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
